shard_granularity_2026-08-10 -- the granularity ladder re-fitted, scored on TAIL
concurrency as well as wall, plus the wide-path collapse it turned out to carry.
Narrative + verdict: docs/SHARD_GRANULARITY.md. This file is provenance only.

WHAT WAS MISSING BEFORE THIS
  `BLOCKS_PER_SHARD = 2` was fitted against WHOLE-FRAME WALL on `v4k_8tile`
  (benchmarks/tracker_blockshift_2026-08-08.meta). docs/TILED_SCALING.md then put
  32-42% of the t=8 wall gap in IDLE CORES, most of it in the post-tile filter
  tail, and named a re-fit "scored on the tail (TAIL_CONC, not whole-frame wall)"
  as the one lever the data points at. Unbuilt until now.
  Separately, benchmarks/strided_2d_2026-08-10.meta refuted the exact strided-2D
  record on `pct_row_wide` -- the fraction of would-be 2-D registrations that
  exceed MAX_SHARDS_PER_BORROW and take ALL 128 shards -- without measuring
  whether any knob moves it.

HOST / BUILD
  Apple M4 Pro (Mac16,11, 8P+4E, 24 GiB), macOS 26.5.2, rustc 1.97.1.
  rav1d-safe perf/shard-granularity, base main @ ca26fd6, release, default
  features except where an arm names a feature. NO -C target-cpu=native.
  dav1d 1.5.4 (homebrew).

  NOT MEASURE-ONLY, unlike the two records above: this branch changes shipped
  code. `BorrowId::PAIR_BITS` is derived (`3 + log2(N_SHARDS)` = 10 at the default
  128 shards) instead of a hardcoded 12, which is a live change in the DEFAULT
  build and is why the corpus gate below covers the default arm and not only the
  ladder rungs. The `bps-*` and `msb-5` features are compile-time A/B arms and
  are OFF by default; `BPS = (2, 1)` reproduces the shipped rule exactly.

ARMS
  plain / tt         default features -- what ships (BPS 2/1)
  bps8  / tt_bps8    BPS 8/1  -> adaptive block shift -2 vs default
  bps4  / tt_bps4    BPS 4/1  -> shift -1
  bps1  / tt_bps1    BPS 1/1  -> shift +1
  bpshalf / tt_bpshalf  BPS 1/2  -> shift +2
  bpsq  / tt_bpsq    BPS 1/4  -> shift +3
  untracked          + probe-untracked (borrow tracker compiled out) -- ceiling
  ttu                + probe-tasktime-untracked
  dav1d_fd1          dav1d --framedelay 1 (matched threading model: our checked
                     build hard-pins n_fc = 1, so frame threading is not an axis
                     we have)

  The `tt*` arms add `probe-tasktime` (per-stage/per-worker busy + the 50 us
  concurrency sampler + TAIL_CONC). That adds a 9th thread on an 8P+4E box, so
  its absolute wall is not comparable with the `plain` family -- it is used only
  for arm-vs-arm comparisons within its own family, which is what the tail
  objective needs.

  LIVENESS of each rung is read off the instances themselves: the `shifts` column
  of the __probe_bounds rect table is the set of block shifts the tracker actually
  used. plain reads 9,11 / 12,14; bpshalf reads 11,13 / 14,16; bpsq 12,14 / 15,17.
  A rung whose shifts equalled the default's did not arm.

VECTORS
  ~/tmp/t8gap/vec/L1024x576_420_8b__t8.avif   1024x576  YUV420 8bpc, 4x2 = 8 tiles,  9 sbrows
  ~/tmp/t8gap/vec/L3840x2160_420_8b__t8.avif  3840x2160 YUV420 8bpc, 4x2 = 8 tiles, 34 sbrows
  controls: L1024x576_420_8b.avif (single tile), and the same 8-tile vector at t=1
  IVF twins in ~/tmp/t8gap/ivf/ (200 frames at 1024x576, 16 at 4K).
  Provenance: benchmarks/size_sweep_t8_gap_2026-08-10.meta + ~/tmp/t8gap/enc_tiles.sh.

  ALL-INTRA, one key-frame OBU re-decoded. No inter prediction, no reference
  management. Loop restoration and super-resolution execute ZERO blocks on both,
  so a null from either here is not a result.

INSTRUMENTS
  1. --features probe-wide (crates/rav1d-disjoint-mut, wide_probe) -- the SHIPPED
     wide-path promotion counts, by door (w_shards / w_blocks / w_full). Timer-free
     and cheap: the three counters fire 10^4-10^5 times per frame. There is
     deliberately no denominator (see `N_ADD`: one shared fetch_add per
     registration at 136 M/frame serialises the decoder hard enough that slot
     pressure disappears and w_full reads zero for the wrong reason).
  2. --features __probe_bounds (bounds_probe::eval_rect) -- the strided-2D
     counterfactual with the instance's REAL geometry. Extended this round:
     pct_wide_c5/c8/c16 (raised-cap counterfactuals) and row_shards_max, and the
     distinct-shard counter widened from 8 to 32 so values above 8 are real
     rather than saturated at 9. At the old cap the question "would a cap of 16
     help?" was unanswerable from the same run.
  3. --features probe-tasktime -- per-stage and per-worker busy ns, the 50 us
     time-weighted concurrency histogram, and TAIL_CONC (the same histogram
     restricted to samples where NO tile worker is live and >= 1 filter worker is).
  4. bash `time` with TIMEFORMAT='%3R %3U %3S' (the child's getrusage), two frame
     counts per cell, total = a + b*frames fitted separately for wall and for
     user+sys, so exec/mmap/decoder-construction/pool-spinup drop out of both.

  INSTRUMENT TRAPS carried over and respected here:
  * At --threads 1 EVERY probe-tasktime stage counter reads 0.000 (n_tc == 1
    creates no task worker, so rav1d_task_run is never entered). The low arm for
    any per-stage ratio is t=2, which is also the better comparison: same code
    path as t=8. t=1 is still the right denominator for a speedup and appears in
    the wall/CPU grid for exactly that.
  * __probe_bounds publishes, fences and scans on every registration (~3.5x
    slower). NO wall-clock number is quoted from any bounds build.
  * n_hi must not exceed the IVF's frame count -- `bench_*` re-decodes one OBU
    exactly n times whatever you ask, `dav1d --limit N` stops at end of stream.
    tiled_wallcpu.sh counts each stream and refuses with a FATAL.

MEASUREMENT HYGIENE
  Every timed run under `measlock` (two holds: shardgran-tail, shardgran-wallcpu),
  rotating arm order inside every cell, medians with min/max bands printed per arm.
  Builds and all counting runs were `nice -n 19`; no timed run was ever niced
  (Darwin maps a positive nice to background QoS -> E-cores).

FILES
  shard_granularity_2026-08-10.txt        the reduced tables (wide, rect, tail, wall/CPU)
  shard_granularity_wide_2026-08-10.txt   raw probe-wide dumps, concatenated
  shard_granularity_rect_2026-08-10.txt   raw __probe_bounds rect tables
  shard_granularity_wallcpu_2026-08-10.tsv  raw wall/CPU rows
  shard_granularity_probe_2026-08-10.tar.zst  raw probe-tasktime dumps

COMMANDS
  scripts/perf/shardgran_build.sh   ~/tmp/shardgran/bin
  PROBES=probe-wide     scripts/perf/shardgran_counts.sh ~/tmp/shardgran/wide
  PROBES=__probe_bounds scripts/perf/shardgran_counts.sh ~/tmp/shardgran/rect
  scripts/perf/shardgran_counts_report.py <dir>
  scripts/perf/shardgran_timed.sh   ~/tmp/shardgran/timed 5 5
  scripts/perf/shardgran_tail_report.py ~/tmp/shardgran/timed/probe
  scripts/perf/tiled_wallcpu_report.py  ~/tmp/shardgran/timed/wallcpu.tsv
